<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.6.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00158</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.6.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0e03e83f-66b6-4daa-a081-ac496b788517</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="75ab0de5-d0d8-464a-8fc5-06a2360884f3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>1. Select three the equations that have the same solution as the equation \(3x-12=24\).</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para>The correct answers are \(15x-60=120,\;3x=36,\;x-4=8\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="dd027593-d07a-43ea-8d5e-67b8b5569b1e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>2. Select three the equations that have the same solution as \(2x-5=15\).</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(2x=20,\;2x-20=0,\;4x-10=30\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6..</para><para>The correct answers are \(2x=20,\;2x-20=0,\;4x-10=30\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="01ada8b9-a708-4ddb-b38d-50d129283b51" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>3. Select four of the equations that are equivalent to: \(x + 0.4x - 4.2 =12.8\).</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.2.</para><para>The correct answers are \(1.4x\;-\;4.2\;=12.8,\;1.4x\;=\;17,\;14x\;-\;42\;=128,\;14x\;=170\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="0331b218-3e9b-45ec-ad25-e6d74a049ed7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>4. Select two of the following that are equivalent to \(3x -6 =12.\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! </para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para>The correct answers are \(3(x-2) = 12\), \(x - 2 =4\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="56557040-0379-48a2-a762-f030812bac8f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>5. Identify which step the mistake is made in finding an equivalent equation to \(2(x - 4) = 16\).</para><para>Step 1: \(2x -4 = 16\)
        Step 2: \(2x =20\)
        Step 3: \(x =10\)</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! Step 1. Distribute the 2 to both terms in the parentheses.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is Step 1 has the mistake.The 2 should be distributed to BOTH terms in the parenthesis. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="75fd1f4b-6ad8-4568-93d1-a1ae87c3c273" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>6. Identify which step the mistake is made in finding an equivalent equation to \(2x +3x -4 = 20\).</para><para>Step 1: \(5x - 4 =20\)
        Step 2: \(5x = 16\)
        Step 3: \(x =16/5\)</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! Step 2. The student should add 4 to both sides of the equation.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is Step 2 has the mistake, The 4 should be ADDED to both sides of the equation. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="c8bf940b-6ba4-4176-aacb-57cb0c1e47c8" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>7. Identify which step the mistake is made in finding an equivalent equation to \(7x - 4x - 5 =16\).</para><para>Step \(1: 3x -5 =16\)
        Step 2: \(3x = 21\)
        Step 3: \(x =62\)</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! Step 3. The student should divide both sides of the equation by 3.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is Step 3 has the mistake. The 3 should be DIVIDED on both sides of the equation. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="e065c300-3340-4075-b263-af12b406a5d8" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>8. Fill in the blank to complete the equivalent equation to 3(x - 5) = 30.</para><para>\(3x\)- ____ =30</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! 15. Distribute the 3 to the 5 with multiplication.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 15. Distribute the 3 to the 5 with multiplication. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="401ce19a-68a6-4497-9c4a-31beacefbf67" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>9. Fill in the blank to complete the equivalent equation to \(\frac x2-5=11\).  .</para><para>\(x\) - ______ = 22</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! 10. Multiply each term in the equation by 2.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para> Correct! 10. Multiply each term in the equation by 2.</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="0df20ed8-b4a3-4125-85ba-698f73c3b8ee" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>10. Fill in the blank to complete the equivalent equation to \( 3(x - 9) = 24\).  .</para><para>\(x\) - ____ = 8</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! 9. Divide both sides of the equation by 3.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.6.3.</para><para>The correct answer is 9. </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
